    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ghent’s roots trace back to 1815 when water‑powered mills sprang up along Yellow Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ghent_ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1849 the town adopted the name Montrose, likely inspired by wild roses that carpeted its rolling hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cfallspainting.com/montrose-ghent-ohio-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ghent’s historic gristmill on Yellow Creek attracted settlers seeking fertile land and water‑powered industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
